### **Q3: Write a program to create an enum for months of a year and print April.**

```c
#include <stdio.h>

enum Month {
    JANUARY, FEBRUARY, MARCH, APRIL, MAY, JUNE,
    JULY, AUGUST, SEPTEMBER, OCTOBER, NOVEMBER, DECEMBER
};

int main() {
    enum Month m = APRIL;

    printf("The selected month is: %d\n", m); // Output will be 3

    return 0;
}
```

> **Note:** Enums start from 0 by default. So `APRIL` has value `3`.

