### **Q4: Write a program to demonstrate typedef.**

```c
#include <stdio.h>

typedef unsigned int uint;

int main() {
    uint a = 10, b = 20;

    printf("a = %u, b = %u\n", a, b);

    return 0;
}
```

> `typedef` is used here to create a new name `uint` for `unsigned int`.

